            <ArticleTitle>A trial of deglycyrrhizinated liquorice in the treatment of duodenal ulcer.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>449-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A double-blind trial of deglycyrrhizinated liquorice was performed in 47 patients with active duodenal ulcer. Twenty-four patients received a placebo and 23 the trial medication (Caved-S) for one month. Both groups were clinically similar. No advantage of deglycyrrhizinated liquorice over placebo was found.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
